program explanation

It's a console-based Java application backed by MySQL.
Main shows the top-level menu; depending on whether the user picks Customer or Admin, control passes to that side's classes.
Customer actions read from menu_items (view/search) or write to orders/order_items/bills (ordering).
Admin actions, after login, write to menu_items/menu_categories (add/update/delete).
Every class talks to the database through the single DBConnecton class, 
so there's one place that owns the connection logic — everything else just runs queries through it. 
That's the whole system: a thin Java layer over a relational schema that models menu → order → bill as a chain of related tables.
